inhibit-charge (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Rename user-facing CLI from "power-mode" to "inhibit-charge".
    The package name and daemon name (inhibit-charged) are unchanged;
    only the command users type changes. Updates the binary path to
    /usr/bin/inhibit-charge and updates all docs and help text.
  * Add "events outside the author's control" clause to disclaimers
    (supply-chain compromise, downstream modifications, AI/LLM output
    in projects that integrate them, third-party service failures).

 -- Ramazan Yavuz <yavuzramazan1994@gmail.com>  Tue, 05 May 2026 14:00:00 +0000

inhibit-charge (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Initial release.
  * Event-driven daemon (udev + SIGHUP + drift timer).
  * Percentage-based hysteresis (max(2, target/10)).
  * home/travel modes with auto-detect of BAT/AC supplies.
  * Hardware capability check at startup.

 -- Ramazan Yavuz <yavuzramazan1994@gmail.com>  Tue, 05 May 2026 12:00:00 +0000
